==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|swait-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|swoid-|lang=ang}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon ''swêt'' (Dutch [[zweet]]), Old High German [[sweiz]] (German [[Schweiß]] ‘sweat’), Old Norse [[sveiti]] ‘sweat, blood’ (Swedish [[svett]], Danish [[sved]]), Sanskrit {{term|स्वेद|sc=Deva|tr=sveda|lang=sa}}. The Indo-European root also gave Latin [[sudor]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/swaːt/|lang=ang}}

